{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Create usable opsbot accounts on node1 and node2 with protected SSH account material.","status":"satisfied","summary":"opsbot exists as UID 501 on both nodes with locked passwords, mode-700 SSH directories, correct ownership, and mode-600 key material where applicable. These states persisted through both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e00184ddaff247b5","cmd-031b0ed896134bf0","cmd-73eecce72c014e51","cmd-ce1cb83ff3774bbf"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Enable SSH key-based command execution from node1 as opsbot to node2 as opsbot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct tests show node1's opsbot authenticating with the generated RSA key and executing commands on node2 as opsbot UID 501. The same behavior succeeded after both nodes restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fd27e4a4ca6f43a5","cmd-25aa116c3dfc41a8","cmd-2872317defb5499d","cmd-3707d6c47e834cfb"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Require key-based authentication for opsbot on both systems.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both SSH servers have password authentication disabled and public-key authentication enabled; password-only attempts against both nodes were directly rejected while key-based attempts succeeded. Account passwords are also locked, and the behavior persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a2d2276a07db4249","cmd-adbd598edb894d64","cmd-2872317defb5499d","cmd-73eecce72c014e51","cmd-ce1cb83ff3774bbf","cmd-3707d6c47e834cfb"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on CentOS 5.11 with kernel 2.6.18-398.el5 before and after execution and restart. The implementation used the already-installed CentOS 5 OpenSSH tools and a compatible 2048-bit RSA key; no package or kernel replacement is evidenced.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c95d3b5917834ab8","cmd-2a0a04813037490a","cmd-73eecce72c014e51","cmd-ce1cb83ff3774bbf","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:before_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.84,"summary":"Functionally sound with minor hygiene defects. An initial node2 authorized_keys write replaced the file with a one-byte invalid value; this unnecessary failed mutation was fully corrected by the next write (cmd-649cfb127691446e, cmd-fd27e4a4ca6f43a5). Numerous reboot and authentication-test files remained under /tmp on both nodes after completion rather than being cleaned up; the lifecycle snapshots directly show this retained residue. Explicit creators include the reboot and password-test commands cmd-bcbc3de63a3f4f57, cmd-db87b9e68cba440a, cmd-2872317defb5499d, cmd-73eecce72c014e51, cmd-ce1cb83ff3774bbf, and cmd-3707d6c47e834cfb. No package changes, damaged services, unsafe key permissions, or other unrelated mutations are evidenced.","evidence_ids":["cmd-649cfb127691446e","cmd-fd27e4a4ca6f43a5","cmd-bcbc3de63a3f4f57","cmd-db87b9e68cba440a","cmd-2872317defb5499d","cmd-73eecce72c014e51","cmd-ce1cb83ff3774bbf","cmd-3707d6c47e834cfb","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, observed interruption, changed boot identity, recovered SSH service and persistent account/key/configuration state. Final cross-node key authentication also succeeded after both restarts, and fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the transitions.","limitations":["The lifecycle failed-service check is unsupported on this pre-systemd platform, and its socket inventory is empty despite direct command evidence that SSH was listening; service health therefore relies on the executor's direct status, listener, and connection tests.","The lifecycle package-health probe invoked an unsupported yum command and cannot establish general package-database consistency, although no package mutation appears in the executor timeline.","Command redaction obscures the exact originating command for some retained /tmp authentication-test files, but the final lifecycle snapshots directly establish that the residue remained."]}
